# Ignore rules for apps/web/Dockerfile, whose build context is the REPO ROOT.
#
# Docker only reads a .dockerignore at the root of the context, so the old
# apps/web/.dockerignore was never applied and `COPY . .` sent every .env file,
# host node_modules and .git into the image. BuildKit reads a file named
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile instead, which is this one.
# Paths are relative to the repo root.

# Secrets. Runtime values come from the platform's secret manager.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Host-built artefacts: wrong platform for the image, and rebuilt inside it.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
tests/e2e/test-results
tests/e2e/playwright-report

# Not part of the web build. tests/e2e stays because its package.json is a
# workspace importer the frozen install expects.
.git
.github
apps/mobile
services
infrastructure
docs
**/.DS_Store
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
